<title>USA: AES unit merger with AES Chigen approved.</title>
<headline>AES unit merger with AES Chigen approved.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>AES Corp said on Thursday that the shareholders of AES China Generating Co Ltd approved its amalgamation with an AES subsidiary.</p>
<p>AES said it expects a certificate of amalgamation shortly from Bermuda, which has jurisdiction over AES Chigen.</p>
<p>AES already owns 48 percent of AES Chigen, which will continue to publicly trade until the certificate is issued.</p>
<p>AES Chigen shareholders were to receive 0.29 AES shares for each AES Chigen share they hold.</p>
</text>
